flowchart TD
    box_0(["Start"])
    box_1{"Does the product meet quality specification?"}
    box_2["Check the input part for correct shape and absence<br/>of burrs."]
    box_3["Remove the non conforming input batch and reload<br/>with parts that meet the required quality<br/>specification."]
    box_4{"Is picking up part from tray correct?"}
    box_5["Follow the input slide pickup diagnostic (GRAPH 17)."]
    box_6[/"Input slide pickup diagnostic (GRAPH 17)"/]
    box_7{"Is picking up part from puck correct?"}
    box_8["Follow the part pickup from carrier puck diagnostic<br/>procedure."]
    box_9[/"Part pickup from carrier puck: diagnostic procedure<br/>reference."/]
    box_10{"Are there contaminated parts?"}
    box_11["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the guide,<br/>fixtures, and optical sensor of the part transfer<br/>holder. 2. Check the rotation mechanism, bearings,<br/>fixtures, and vacuum system of the reorientation<br/>mechanism."]
    box_12["Clean the contaminated parts and lubricate the<br/>actuator guide"]
    box_13{"Are there electrical defects?"}
    box_14["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the height<br/>proximity sensor and vacuum valve of the<br/>reorientation mechanism. 2. Check the height<br/>proximity sensor, mounting cylinder valve, and part<br/>present proximity sensor of the part transfer<br/>holder. 3. Check the position indicators of the<br/>reversing actuator."]
    box_15["Adjust or replace the defective electrical component<br/>identified in the inspection (proximity sensor,<br/>valve, or position indicator)."]
    box_16{"Are there worn parts?"}
    box_17["Complete the following checks: 1. Check the rotation<br/>mechanism, rotation actuator, and associated valve<br/>of the reorientation mechanism. 2. Check the<br/>mounting actuator and its valve. 3. Check the<br/>fixtures of the part transfer holder and the<br/>reorientation mechanism."]
    box_18["Replace the worn components identified in the<br/>inspection (rotation mechanism, rotation actuator,<br/>mounting actuator, and/or fixture)."]
    box_19{"Are the stops of the reorientation mechanism<br/>correctly adjusted?"}
    box_20[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_21[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_22[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_23{"Are the stops of the reorientation mechanism<br/>correctly adjusted?"}
    box_24[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_25[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_26[/"Refer to the reorientation mechanism stop adjustment<br/>for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_27["Adjust the stops of the reorientation mechanism to<br/>the correct position per the process specification<br/>for the current machine variant."]
    box_28{"Are the stops of the part transfer holder correctly<br/>adjusted?"}
    box_29[/"Refer to the part transfer holder stop adjustment<br/>for variant A machines (small format parts)."/]
    box_30[/"Refer to the part transfer holder stop adjustment<br/>for variant B machines (medium format parts)."/]
    box_31[/"Refer to the part transfer holder stop adjustment<br/>for variant C machines (large format parts)."/]
    box_32["Adjust the stops of the part transfer holder to the<br/>correct position per the process specification for<br/>the current machine variant."]
    box_33["Verify that parts are picked up centred under the<br/>vacuum end effectors and are not dropped during<br/>transport."]
    box_34(["Placing part in reorientation mechanism (input) is<br/>correct"])

